IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`

-- Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) -- cases for the seat-neutral core (rtw-core.l4) and the dates module (rtw-dates.l4).
--
-- An illustrative worker, Mia: a full-time storeperson (38 hours a week) at a warehouse in Adelaide, employed by a company
-- that is registered with ReturnToWorkSA and is not self-insured. Born 14 May 1990. She hurts her back lifting on Monday
-- 2 March 2026 (age 35) and tells her supervisor three hours later. Her incapacity for work first occurs on Tuesday 3
-- March 2026 (day 0 of her designated periods) and she gives her claim, with her doctor's certificate, on Tuesday 10 March
-- 2026. Her age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) is 67 (804 months).
-- ILLUSTRATIVE figures, not from any deposit: the CPI (Adelaide, All groups) for the September quarter before the
-- adjustment 125.4, and for the base September quarter 100.0 (a factor of 1.254); State average weekly earnings $1,900;
-- the Federal minimum wage $915.90 a week; the prime bank rate 7.8%. Monday 9 March 2026 is Adelaide Cup Day, given here
-- as one weekday public holiday where it falls in a period (the State's public holidays are not deposited).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above it.
-- A breached DEONTIC satisfies neither `EQUALS FULFILLED` nor its negation on the stable l4, so breaches and open
-- obligations are #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line. Clock: days (hours for the s 16 rule).

`the illustrative CPI` MEANS
    `CPI figures` WITH
        `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS 125.4
        `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS 100

`no indexation` MEANS
    `CPI figures` WITH
        `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS 100
        `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS 100

`Mia's first day of incapacity` MEANS `the calendar date` 3 3 2026

§ `Dates`

-- s 4(1) business days: Monday 2 March 2026 plus 5 business days is Monday 9 March; Adelaide Cup Day (9 March) pushes it
-- to Tuesday 10 March. From Tuesday 10 March: 11, 12, 13, 16, 17 March.
#ASSERT `the last of` 5 `business days after` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `with public holidays` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 9 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 5 `business days after` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `with public holidays` 1 EQUALS `the calendar date` 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 5 `business days after` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) `with public holidays` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 17 3 2026
-- The period of 6 months commencing on 3 March 2026 ends on 2 September 2026; commencing on 31 August 2026, it ends on
-- 28 February 2027 (no 31 February); on 28 August, on 27 February.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 6 `months commencing on` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 2 9 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 6 `months commencing on` (`the calendar date` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of` 6 `months commencing on` (`the calendar date` 28 8 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 27 2 2027
-- Designated periods from 3 March 2026: day 363 (1 March 2027) is in the first; day 364 (2 March 2027) the second; day
-- 727 (28 February 2028) the second; day 728 (29 February 2028, a leap day) is after the 104 weeks.
#ASSERT `the designated period of` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) `counted from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the designated period of` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2027) `counted from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the designated period of` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2028) `counted from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the designated period of` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) `counted from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the designated period of` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `counted from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` EQUALS 0
-- Age: Mia (born 14 May 1990) is 35 on 2 March 2026 and 36 on 14 May 2026.
#ASSERT `the age in whole years of a person born on` (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) `on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `the age in whole years of a person born on` (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) `on` (`the calendar date` 14 5 2026) EQUALS 36

§ `Indexed amounts (s 4(17), regs 4, 8)`

-- Reg 25 $2 374 x 1.254 = 2976.996, rounded up to $2 977. Reg 35(3) $10 172 x 1.254 = 12755.688, up to $12 756. s 57
-- $472 000 x 1.254 = $591 888 exactly. With no change in the CPI, the stated sum.
#ASSERT 2374 `indexed by` `the illustrative CPI` EQUALS 2977
#ASSERT 10172 `indexed by` `the illustrative CPI` EQUALS 12756
#ASSERT 472000 `indexed by` `the illustrative CPI` EQUALS 591888
#ASSERT 2374 `indexed by` `no indexation` EQUALS 2374

§ `Am I a worker (s 4, regs 5, 6)`

`an engagement` MEANS
    `Engagement facts` WITH
        `employed by the other person`                                             IS FALSE
        `an apprentice or trainee under a contract of apprenticeship`              IS FALSE
        `paid while receiving on-the-job training in a trade or vocation from the other person` IS FALSE
        `the class of work`                                                        IS `none of the regulation 5 classes`
        `the work is done for the purposes of the other person's trade or business` IS TRUE
        `the work is done personally`                                              IS TRUE
        `someone else is employed to do part of the work`                          IS FALSE
        `the value of the materials supplied`                                      IS 0
        `the total payable under the arrangement`                                  IS 0
        `the value of the most valuable tool or item of plant or equipment`        IS 0
        `the term of the arrangement in months`                                    IS 1
        `more than 1 vehicle is owned or operated for work at the same time`       IS FALSE
        `the goods are or were owned by the driver or by the other person`         IS FALSE
        `the vehicle is supplied by the other person or someone related to it`     IS FALSE
        `a fishing crew member paid by a share of profits or gross receipts`       IS FALSE
        `a volunteer of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer under Schedule 1` IS FALSE
        `the Corporation has extended the Act's protection to the person under s 175` IS FALSE
        `the regulation 6 class`                                                   IS `none of the regulation 6 classes`

-- A contractor in none of the reg 5 classes, not employed: not a worker.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker` `an engagement` `the illustrative CPI`)
`an employment` MEANS
    `Engagement facts` WITH
        `employed by the other person`                                             IS TRUE
        `an apprentice or trainee under a contract of apprenticeship`              IS FALSE
        `paid while receiving on-the-job training in a trade or vocation from the other person` IS FALSE
        `the class of work`                                                        IS `none of the regulation 5 classes`
        `the work is done for the purposes of the other person's trade or business` IS TRUE
        `the work is done personally`                                              IS TRUE
        `someone else is employed to do part of the work`                          IS FALSE
        `the value of the materials supplied`                                      IS 0
        `the total payable under the arrangement`                                  IS 0
        `the value of the most valuable tool or item of plant or equipment`        IS 0
        `the term of the arrangement in months`                                    IS 1
        `more than 1 vehicle is owned or operated for work at the same time`       IS FALSE
        `the goods are or were owned by the driver or by the other person`         IS FALSE
        `the vehicle is supplied by the other person or someone related to it`     IS FALSE
        `a fishing crew member paid by a share of profits or gross receipts`       IS FALSE
        `a volunteer of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer under Schedule 1` IS FALSE
        `the Corporation has extended the Act's protection to the person under s 175` IS FALSE
        `the regulation 6 class`                                                   IS `none of the regulation 6 classes`

-- Mia, employed: a worker (contract of service (a)).
#ASSERT `the person is a worker` `an employment` `the illustrative CPI`

§ `Is my injury a work injury (s 7)`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of injury`
GIVETH AN `Injury facts`
`Mia's injury as` k MEANS
    `Injury facts` WITH
        `the kind of injury`                                                     IS k
        `it arose out of or in the course of employment`                         IS TRUE
        `employment was a significant contributing cause`                        IS TRUE
        `employment was the significant contributing cause`                      IS FALSE
        `it arose wholly or predominantly from reasonable action or decisions of the kinds in s 7(4)` IS FALSE
        `it arose from a social or sporting activity`                            IS FALSE
        `the activity was part of the employment or at the employer's direction or request` IS FALSE
        `it arose on a journey`                                                  IS FALSE
        `the journey was in the course of carrying out duties of employment`     IS FALSE
        `the journey was between places listed in s 7(8)(b)`                     IS FALSE
        `the route was reasonably direct without a substantial, riskier deviation` IS FALSE
        `there is a real and substantial connection between the employment and the journey` IS FALSE

-- s 7(2)(a): in the course of employment, and employment "a" significant contributing cause.
#ASSERT `the injury arises from employment` (`Mia's injury as` `a physical injury`)
-- s 7(2)(b): the same facts for a psychiatric injury fail, because employment must be "the" significant contributing cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`the injury arises from employment` (`Mia's injury as` `a psychiatric injury`))

§ `Notice and claim (ss 16, 30; regs 11, 19)`

#ASSERT `to whom notice of the injury must be given` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the employer by whom the worker was employed when the injury occurred`
#ASSERT `to whom notice of the injury must be given` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Corporation`
#ASSERT `to whom notice of the injury must be given` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Corporation`
#ASSERT `the hours within which notice should be given` TRUE 0 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `the hours within which notice should be given` FALSE 60 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `notice given this way is taken to have been given to the employer` `by email to an address the employer uses in the ordinary course of business`
#ASSERT NOT (`notice given this way is taken to have been given to the employer` `in some other way`)
-- Mia's entitlement arises on 3 March 2026: the last day is 2 September 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to make the claim` `Mia's first day of incapacity` EQUALS `the calendar date` 2 9 2026
#ASSERT `the claim was made within the prescribed period` `Mia's first day of incapacity` (`the calendar date` 2 9 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the claim was made within the prescribed period` `Mia's first day of incapacity` (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026))
#ASSERT `to whom the claim must be given` TRUE EQUALS `the employer`
#ASSERT `who may certify the claim` `a nurse practitioner who examined the worker at an incorporated or private hospital` EQUALS `a designated person may certify the claim, but the capacity certified covers only the next 7 days`
-- s 30(5): Mia's claim, received Tuesday 10 March 2026, must be forwarded by Tuesday 17 March.
#ASSERT `the employer's 5 business days after receiving it on` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) `with public holidays` 0 `self-insured` FALSE EQUALS `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` (`the calendar date` 17 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the employer's 5 business days after receiving it on` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) `with public holidays` 0 `self-insured` TRUE EQUALS `no duty to forward: the employer is a self-insured employer`
-- ss 31(4), 32(2): received by the Corporation on Tuesday 17 March 2026; the 10th business day after is Tuesday 31 March.
#ASSERT `the 10th business day after the Corporation received the claim on` (`the calendar date` 17 3 2026) `with public holidays` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty under ss 16(6), 30(5) and 30(6)` EQUALS 1500

§ `Average weekly earnings (s 5, regs 7, 9)`

-- Earnings facts: the period's earnings, non-cash benefits, overtime expected, award wage (0 for none), self-employed, hours.
GIVEN `the period's earnings` IS A NUMBER, `the non-cash benefits` IS A NUMBER, `overtime expected` IS A BOOLEAN, `the award wage` IS A NUMBER, se IS A BOOLEAN, `the hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earnings facts`
`earnings of` `the period's earnings` `with benefits` `the non-cash benefits` `overtime` `overtime expected` `award` `the award wage` `self-employed` se `hours` `the hours` MEANS
    `Earnings facts` WITH
        `the earnings in the relevant period, other than overtime`         IS `the period's earnings`
        `the weeks in the relevant period`                                 IS 52
        `the weekly value of prescribed non-cash benefits not retained`     IS `the non-cash benefits`
        `a reasonable expectation of working overtime`                     IS `overtime expected`
        `the overtime component`                                           IS 100
        `the pay was covered by an award or industrial agreement`          IS `the award wage` GREATER THAN 0
        `the weekly wage under the award or industrial agreement`          IS `the award wage`
        `a self-employed worker`                                           IS se
        `the hours worked per week`                                        IS `the hours`
        `the hours per week that constitute full-time employment`          IS 38
        `the Federal minimum wage per week`                                IS 915.90
        `State average weekly earnings`                                    IS 1900

-- 65 000 / 52 = 1 250; + 50 (a car she does not keep, reg 9(i)) + 100 overtime component = 1 400; above the award $1 000
-- and the minimum wage; under 2 x 1 900 = 3 800.
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings under s 5` (`earnings of` 65000 `with benefits` 50 `overtime` TRUE `award` 1000 `self-employed` FALSE `hours` 38) EQUALS 1400
-- No reasonable expectation of overtime (s 5(12)(a)): 1 300.
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings under s 5` (`earnings of` 65000 `with benefits` 50 `overtime` FALSE `award` 1000 `self-employed` FALSE `hours` 38) EQUALS 1300
-- A high earner, 260 000 / 52 = 5 000 + 150: capped at 3 800 (s 5(15)(c)).
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings under s 5` (`earnings of` 260000 `with benefits` 50 `overtime` TRUE `award` 1000 `self-employed` FALSE `hours` 38) EQUALS 3800
-- Reg 7(2): 20 hours of 38 is 52.63..%, 52.6% to 1 decimal point; 915.90 x 52.6% = 481.7634.
#ASSERT `the Federal minimum wage for` 20 `hours of` 38 `from` 915.90 EQUALS 481.7634
-- A part-time worker averaging $400 (20 800 / 52), no award: fixed at the pro-rata minimum wage, 481.7634 (s 5(15)(b));
-- if self-employed, the floor does not apply: 400.
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings under s 5` (`earnings of` 20800 `with benefits` 0 `overtime` FALSE `award` 0 `self-employed` FALSE `hours` 20) EQUALS 481.7634
#ASSERT `the average weekly earnings under s 5` (`earnings of` 20800 `with benefits` 0 `overtime` FALSE `award` 0 `self-employed` TRUE `hours` 20) EQUALS 400

§ `Weekly payments (ss 36-44)`

#ASSERT `the work capacity of a worker` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a current work capacity`
#ASSERT `the work capacity of a worker` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no current work capacity`
#ASSERT `the work capacity of a worker` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not incapacitated for work`

-- Weekly payment facts: seriously injured, capacity, first day of incapacity, day asked about, NWE, current earnings.
GIVEN `seriously injured` IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A `Work capacity`, `the first day` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Weekly payment facts`
`a week` `seriously injured` c `from` `the first day` `on` `the day` `NWE` n `earning` d MEANS
    `Weekly payment facts` WITH
        `paid as a seriously injured worker`        IS `seriously injured`
        `the work capacity`                         IS c
        `the day incapacity first occurred`          IS `the first day`
        `the day asked about`                        IS `the day`
        `notional weekly earnings`                   IS n
        `designated weekly earnings`                 IS d
        `the Federal minimum wage for the worker`    IS 915.90

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Weekly payment facts`
`Mia's week on` `the day` MEANS `a week` FALSE `no current work capacity` `from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` `on` `the day` `NWE` 1400 `earning` 0

-- s 39(1)(a)(i): first 52 weeks, no current work capacity: 1 400.
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`Mia's week on` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026)) EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1400
-- s 39(1)(a)(ii): 1 June 2026, back part-time earning 600: 1 400 - 600 = 800.
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`a week` FALSE `a current work capacity` `from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` `on` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) `NWE` 1400 `earning` 600) EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 800
-- s 39(1)(b)(i): 2 March 2027 (day 364): 80% of 1 400 = 1 120. The day before: 1 400.
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`Mia's week on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2027)) EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1120
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`Mia's week on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027)) EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1400
-- s 39(3): 29 February 2028 (day 728): nothing. As a seriously injured worker (s 41(1)(b)): 1 120.
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`Mia's week on` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028)) EQUALS `no weekly payment: more than 104 weeks after the incapacity first occurred (s 39(3))`
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`a week` TRUE `no current work capacity` `from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` `on` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) `NWE` 1400 `earning` 0) EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1120
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`a week` FALSE `not incapacitated for work` `from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` `on` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) `NWE` 1400 `earning` 0) EQUALS `no weekly payment: not incapacitated for work`
-- s 42 (finding 9): a worker on the minimum wage, NWE 915.90, in the second 52 weeks: 80% is 732.72, raised to 915.90; with
-- current earnings of 400, 80% of 515.90 is 412.72 and the combined 812.72 is raised to 915.90, so the payment is 515.90.
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`a week` FALSE `no current work capacity` `from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` `on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2027) `NWE` 915.90 `earning` 0) EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 915.90
#ASSERT `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` (`a week` FALSE `a current work capacity` `from` `Mia's first day of incapacity` `on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2027) `NWE` 915.90 `earning` 400) EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 515.90
-- s 41(3): an assessment on 1 June 2026; 26 July is day 55 (still within 8 weeks), 27 July day 56 (not).
#ASSERT `the day is within 8 weeks of the assessment` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 26 7 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the day is within 8 weeks of the assessment` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 27 7 2026))
-- Reg 27: 1 July 2026 is a Wednesday, so the adjustment is on Sunday 5 July 2026; 1 July 2029 is a Sunday.
#ASSERT `the day the s 42 Federal minimum wage is adjusted in` 2026 EQUALS `the calendar date` 5 7 2026
#ASSERT `the day the s 42 Federal minimum wage is adjusted in` 2029 EQUALS `the calendar date` 1 7 2029

-- Retiring age facts: date of birth, normal retiring age in months (0 for none), first day of incapacity, still employed.
GIVEN `the birthday` IS A DATE, `the normal age` IS A NUMBER, `the first day` IS A DATE, emp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Retiring age facts`
`retiring facts born` `the birthday` `normal age` `the normal age` `first incapacity` `the first day` `employed` emp MEANS
    `Retiring age facts` WITH
        `the date of birth`                                           IS `the birthday`
        `there is a normal retiring age for the kind of employment`   IS `the normal age` GREATER THAN 0
        `the normal retiring age, in months`                          IS `the normal age`
        `the age pension age, in months`                              IS 804
        `the day incapacity first occurred`                           IS `the first day`
        `still in employment when the incapacity first occurred`      IS emp

`Mia's retiring age facts` MEANS `retiring facts born` (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) `normal age` 0 `first incapacity` `Mia's first day of incapacity` `employed` TRUE

-- s 44: Mia reaches 67 on 14 May 2057. Not a seriously injured worker: s 39(3) ends payments first, on 28 February 2028
-- (day 727). Seriously injured: 14 May 2057.
#ASSERT `the s 44 answer for` `Mia's retiring age facts` EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 14 5 2057)
#ASSERT `the last day of weekly payments for` `Mia's retiring age facts` `if seriously injured` FALSE EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2028)
#ASSERT `the last day of weekly payments for` `Mia's retiring age facts` `if seriously injured` TRUE EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 14 5 2057)
-- Peter, born 1 July 1960, a normal retiring age of 70 in his work, so his retiring age is the lesser, 67: 1 July 2027.
-- Incapacitated while still employed on 2 March 2026, within 2 years of it (from 1 July 2025): s 44(3) pays 104 weeks, to
-- 27 February 2028 (2 March 2026 + 727 days), past his retiring age (finding 11).
`Peter's retiring age facts` MEANS `retiring facts born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) `normal age` 840 `first incapacity` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `employed` TRUE
#ASSERT `the retiring age in months for` `Peter's retiring age facts` EQUALS 804
#ASSERT `s 44(3) applies to` `Peter's retiring age facts`
#ASSERT `the s 44 answer for` `Peter's retiring age facts` EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 27 2 2028)
-- A seriously injured worker born 1 June 1962 (retiring age 1 June 2029), first incapacitated 2 March 2026, more than 2
-- years before it: paid until 1 June 2029, and nothing on 2 June 2029 (s 44(2)).
`Sam's retiring age facts` MEANS `retiring facts born` (`the calendar date` 1 6 1962) `normal age` 0 `first incapacity` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `employed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44(3) applies to` `Sam's retiring age facts`)
#ASSERT `the weekly payment on the day for` (`a week` TRUE `no current work capacity` `from` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `on` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2029) `NWE` 1400 `earning` 0) `with retiring age facts` `Sam's retiring age facts` EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1120
#ASSERT `the weekly payment on the day for` (`a week` TRUE `no current work capacity` `from` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `on` (`the calendar date` 2 6 2029) `NWE` 1400 `earning` 0) `with retiring age facts` `Sam's retiring age facts` EQUALS `no weekly payment: after the worker reached retiring age (s 44(2))`
-- Above retiring age and not in employment when incapacitated: no weekly payments at all.
#ASSERT `the s 44 answer for` (`retiring facts born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) `normal age` 840 `first incapacity` (`the calendar date` 1 8 2027) `employed` FALSE) EQUALS `no weekly payments: the worker had already reached retiring age and was not in employment`

§ `Supplementary income support (s 40, reg 26)`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, appr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Supplementary facts`
`Mia's surgery, asked on` `the day` `approved` appr MEANS
    `Supplementary facts` WITH
        `the weekly facts`                          IS `Mia's week on` `the day`
        `the surgery was approved by the Corporation` IS appr
        `the day of the surgery`                    IS `the calendar date` 1 5 2028

`the reg 26 CPI` MEANS
    `CPI figures` WITH
        `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS 140
        `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS 135

